<title>FINLAND: IBCA RATES UHISPANK SHORT-TERM DEBT &quot;2&quot;.</title>
<headline>IBCA RATES UHISPANK SHORT-TERM DEBT &quot;2&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian bank Eesti Uhispank said on Tuesday that international credit rating agency IBCA had issued on May 23 a &quot;2&quot; rating for its short-term debt.</p>
<p>Uhispank said in a statement this was a strong achievement by the bank since a number &quot;1&quot; rating could only be given to banks guaranteed by governments.</p>
<p>&quot;Uhispank estimates that getting a good short-term debt rating creates an opportunity to get also a good long-term debt rating,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Uhispank is Estonia's second largest bank.</p>
<p>IBCA has been active in the Baltic region, assiging a rating to Lithuania earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
